trophic events, may result in significant disruption in the credit markets, which may adversely affect our ability to refinance existing debt or obtain additional financing to support operations or to fund new acquisitions or capital-intensive internal initiatives.","context":"Changes in our credit ratings or macroeconomic impacts on credit markets may increase our cost of capital and limit financing options.","section":"Damage to our reputation or brand could negatively impact our business, financial condition or results of operations.","block":221,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000818479-26-000075","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000818479","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/818479/000081847926000075/xray-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/6db2c807353a73423e333d391abca480b61440b3d4beabd25f58ed9628810233.bin","sha256":"6db2c807353a73423e333d391abca480b61440b3d4beabd25f58ed9628810233"}},{"id":"6819ae6543d6e6a3990de10c497ffe99622cbcd9a217bd186e33b4bcd34afb64","quote":"Any adverse changes in our credit ratings may result in increased borrowing costs for future long-term debt or short-term borrowing facilities which may in turn limit financing options, including access to the unsecured borrowing market. There is no guarantee that additional debt financing will be available in the future to fund obligations, or that it will be available on commercially reasonable terms, in which case we may need to seek other sources of funding.","context":"We utilize short- and long-term debt markets to obtain capital from time to time. Our continued access to sources of liquidity depends on multiple factors, including global economic conditions, the condition of global credit markets, the availability of sufficient amounts of financing, operating performance, and credit ratings. Macroeconomic impacts, including natural disasters, pandemics, geopolitical conditions or other catastrophic events, may result in significant disruption in the credit markets, which may adversely affect our ability to refinance existing debt or obtain additional financing to support operations or to fund new acquisitions or capital-intensive internal initiatives.","section":"Damage to our reputation or brand could negatively impact our business, financial condition or results of operations.","block":222,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000818479-26-000075","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000818479","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/818479/000081847926000075/xray-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/6db2c807353a73423e333d391abca480b61440b3d4beabd25f58ed9628810233.bin","sha256":"6db2c807353a73423e333d391abca480b61440b3d4beabd25f58ed9628810233"}},{"id":"3e1ee05984946dcfeccb5e6a43da496789d2e77b6a55c3989b702fdfe20d646d","quote":"Our indebtedness could adversely affect our financial condition and prevent us from fulfilling our debt or contractual obligations.","context":"Any adverse changes in our credit ratings may result in increased borrowing costs for future long-term debt or short-term borrowing facilities which may in turn limit financing options, including access to the unsecured borrowing market. There is no guarantee that additional debt financing will be available in the future to fund obligations, or that it will be available on commercially reasonable terms, in which case we may need to seek other sources of funding.","section":"Damage to our reputation or brand could negatively impact our business, financial condition or results of operations.","block":223,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000818479-26-000075","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000818479","url"